<http://data.silknow.org/object/c6e57e87-863c-3653-a806-0f49c74e7455>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Veil for Communion vessels. Eastern Orthodox Church. The baby Jesus, on a patten, a chalice and the Bible (?) all on an altar over which a canopy is supported by four columns and a censer is suspended. Standing on either side the Archangels Gabriel and Michael. All metallic yarns except flesh and hair areas being silk worked in split stitch; on a red satin silk ground. Narrow metallic silk and linen yarn tape border. Tassel pendant from three of the corners."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e7727376-eda9-358d-8476-d8f2be47805b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Veil for Communion vessels. Eastern Orthodox Church. The baby Jesus, on a patten, a chalice and the Bible (?) all on an altar over which a canopy is supported by four columns and a censer is suspended. Standing on either side the Archangels Gabriel and Michael. All metallic yarns except flesh and hair areas being silk worked in split stitch; on a red satin silk ground. Narrow metallic silk and linen yarn tape border. Tassel pendant from three of the corners."@en ;
